//! `NEIGHBORHOOD_SIZE` slots starting at `i` currently hold an entry whose home bucket is `i`.
//! The entry slot itself is independent of the bitmap: bucket `i`'s `entry` may belong to some
//! earlier home bucket `i - k`.
//!
//! Layout of [`Bucket::infos`] (a `u64`):
//!
//! ```text
//!  bit 63          bit 62        bits 61..0
//! +--------+-------------------+-----------------------------------+
//! | unused | overflow present  | neighborhood presence bitmap      |
//! +--------+-------------------+-----------------------------------+
//! ```
//!
//! Bit `j` of the neighborhood bitmap (`j` in `0..NEIGHBORHOOD_SIZE`) means "the slot at
//! `self_index + j` holds an entry whose home bucket is `self_index`".  The overflow bit means
